### Essay Drafts API — ready-made requests
### In VS Code, install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request"
### above any request. Start the server first with: npm start

@base = http://localhost:3000

### Is the server up?
GET {{base}}/

### Create a draft (the server calculates word_count itself)
POST {{base}}/drafts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My argumentative essay",
  "content": "Technology has changed how students write and revise their work."
}

### List all drafts
GET {{base}}/drafts

### Get one draft
GET {{base}}/drafts/1

### Replace a draft
PUT {{base}}/drafts/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My argumentative essay (revised)",
  "content": "Technology has deeply changed how students draft, revise and reflect."
}

### Delete a draft
DELETE {{base}}/drafts/1

### Error case: missing title -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{base}}/drafts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "No title here"
}

### Error case: unknown id -> 404 Not Found
GET {{base}}/drafts/9999
